  "shared_implementation": "All declared language services use the same process primitive and shared command workflow in both authenticated transports. Linux/macOS run an independent watcher through a private mode in the matching bridge executable. The original server keeps its declared program, arguments, environment, working directory and direct inherited stdio.",
  "behavior": "Before approved command dispatch, the existing folder lease passes its complete directory lock set to that service watcher. Acknowledged command completion releases the loan and preserves the warm server. Lost control, signals or server exit stop the original managed process group. The watcher retains the unreaped child identity and directory descriptors until the group is confirmed quiescent, then closes descriptors before reaping.",
  "bounds": {
    "control_protocol": 1,
    "control_body_bytes": 4194304,
    "passed_directory_descriptors": 64,
    "control_io_timeout_seconds": 2,
    "process_cleanup_observer_timeout_seconds": 3,
    "cleanup_retention": "Failed or incomplete cleanup retains the physical locks without an age-based takeover.",
    "linux_inventory_limit": 65536,
    "macos_group_inventory_limit": 4096,
    "runtime": "One watcher per language service, no Tokio runtime in the watcher. Resource sampling includes the watcher as the original process-tree root."
  },
